              "text": "I've completed my review. Here's the full plan:\n\n---\n\n## OpenClaw Tailscale Deployment Plan\n\n### What the Playbook Does\n\nThe `playbooks/openclaw.yml` builds a custom Docker image that:\n1. **Builds OpenClaw from source** (clones the GitHub repo, installs deps, compiles)\n2. **Adds Tailscale** to the container image\n3. **Runs Tailscale daemon inside the container** with `NET_ADMIN` capabilities\n4. **Authenticates to your tailnet** using an auth key from vault\n5. **Container hostname**: `openclaw-gateway` on the tailnet\n\n### Prerequisites Checklist\n\n| Item | Status | Action |\n|------|--------|--------|\n| `vault_tailscale_auth_key` | **Required** | Generate at https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys |\n| `vault_anthropic_api_key` | Likely exists | Already running, should be in vault |\n| `vault_openclaw_gateway_token` | Likely exists | Already running, should be in vault |\n| `vault_google_oauth_client_id` | Optional | For Google integration |\n| `vault_google_oauth_client_secret` | Optional | For Google integration |\n| `proxy` Docker network | Required | Should already exist for other services |\n\n### Before Running: Verify Vault Has Tailscale Key\n\n```bash\ncd ~/tower-control\nansible-vault view vars/vault.yml --ask-vault-pass | grep tailscale\n```\n\nIf `vault_tailscale_auth_key` is missing, you need to:\n\n1. **Generate a Tailscale auth key:**\n   - Go to https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys\n   - Create new key with: **reusable=true**, **ephemeral=false**, **tags=tag:servers** (if using ACLs)\n\n2. **Add to vault:**\n   ```bash\n   ansible-vault edit vars/vault.yml --ask-vault-pass\n   # Add line: vault_tailscale_auth_key: \"tskey-auth-xxxxxxxxxxxx\"\n   ```\n\n### Deployment Commands\n\n**Step 1: Dry run (recommended)**\n```bash\ncd ~/tower-control\nansible-playbook -i inventory/hosts.yml playbooks/openclaw.yml --ask-vault-pass --check\n```\n\n**Step 2: Deploy**\n```bash\nansible-playbook -i inventory/hosts.yml playbooks/openclaw.yml --ask-vault-pass\n```\n\nThe build will take a few minutes (clones repo, installs pnpm deps, compiles TypeScript).\n\n### Post-Deployment Verification\n\nFrom tower (SSH):\n```bash\n# Check container is running\ndocker ps | grep openclaw\n\n# Check Tailscale connected inside container\ndocker exec openclaw-app tailscale status\n\n# Test it can reach internal services\ndocker exec openclaw-app curl -s https://actual.coyne.sh | head -5\n```\n\n### Risks & Considerations\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|------|------------|\n| **Downtime during rebuild** | Container rebuilds from source (~3-5 min). Main agent will disconnect. |\n| **Lost state** | Workspace dirs are mounted (`/mnt/user/appdata/openclaw`), data persists. Tailscale state in Docker volume. |\n| **Auth key exposure** | Key is in vault (encrypted) and passed as env var. Don't echo `docker inspect`. |\n| **ACL issues** | If you use Tailscale ACLs, ensure `tag:servers` or `openclaw-gateway` can reach your services. |\n\n### What Changes\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| OpenClaw can only reach public internet | OpenClaw can reach `*.coyne.sh` services via Tailscale |\n| Container has no tailnet presence | Container appears as `openclaw-gateway` on tailnet |\n| Groundskeeper can't manage local services | Full access to Actual Budget, Home Assistant, etc. |\n\n---\n\n**TL;DR Commands:**\n```bash\n# 1. Verify vault has tailscale key\nansible-vault view vars/vault.yml --ask-vault-pass | grep tailscale\n\n# 2. If missing, add it\nansible-vault edit vars/vault.yml --ask-vault-pass\n\n# 3. Deploy\ncd ~/tower-control\nansible-playbook -i inventory/hosts.yml playbooks/openclaw.yml --ask-vault-pass\n```"
